# Cursor adapter

Read `AGENTS.md` for the canonical safety, protection and intent-first contract.
Classify intent first: advice, review-only and plan-only never start or resume
runtime delivery, even with a FlutterCrew keyword or selected delivery entrypoint.
Otherwise quick direct assistance is the default; explicitly activated
implementation follows `.agents/workflows/feature-delivery.md`.

For that delivery use `.agents/workflows/input-intake.md`: accept direct prompts
or optional documents, preserve existing runs/briefs, never overwrite or reset.
The shared workflow owns approval, traceability, verify → accept → finish ordering
and proportional standard/full spec/test scope; do not copy a separate pipeline.

Protection applies in installed target apps, not maintenance of the FlutterCrew
source repository. Never edit active state or recorded evidence directly.
Use only host-supported tools. Role guides are not native agent registrations;
when delegation is unavailable use honest sequential role passes and host model
defaults. Read shared files explicitly if the host does not discover them.
